-- The proto and the three-layer spawn fill. Twin of s61-proto-spawn.bqn.
-- Two grunts and a barracks order. def Marine is the archetype — the proto — and a spawned row fills proto-first, registered-default second, type-zero last.
-- `def Marine soldier=1 hp=100` registers the archetype; `spawn Marine` fills each column through the ruled three-layer lookup — the proto's value (soldier 1, hp 100), else the registered default (ammo 5), else the type zero (gold 0). The unique id column never takes a layer: injectivity forces a fresh mint (1+max), and the proto-role sym column records the archetype's noun.
-- One soldier selects, one Marine lands: row 2, id 6.
--! registry ../registries/s61-proto-spawn.reg
--! expect-n 3
--! expect id = 3 5 6
--! expect soldier = 1 0 1
--! expect hp = 40 10 100
--! expect ammo = 7 7 5
--! expect gold = 100 200 0
--! expect proto = Grunt Grunt Marine

Soldier , spawn Marine
